<qti-assessment-item xmlns="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/imsqtiasi_v3p0" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/imsqtiasi_v3p0 https://purl.imsglobal.org/spec/qti/v3p0/schema/xsd/imsqti_asiv3p0_v1p0.xsd" identifier="pcb-item-8d785e515faa4b09a2ba24a9327dc5dc" title="sat-c1-u04-treatise.html qc2" adaptive="true" time-dependent="false">
  <qti-response-declaration identifier="RESPONSE" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier">
    <qti-correct-response><qti-value>D</qti-value></qti-correct-response>
  </qti-response-declaration>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="SCORE" cardinality="single" base-type="float"><qti-default-value><qti-value>0</qti-value></qti-default-value></qti-outcome-declaration>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="FEEDBACK" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier"/>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="INTERACTION_VISIBILITY" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier">
    <qti-default-value><qti-value>show_interaction</qti-value></qti-default-value>
  </qti-outcome-declaration>
  <qti-item-body>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="show_interaction" outcome-identifier="INTERACTION_VISIBILITY" show-hide="show" class="qti-margin-0">
      <qti-content-body>
        <p>For the alumni magazine, the retired coach wrote a wandering eight-page ____ on locker-room speeches — personal, funny, and happy to chase a memory wherever it led.</p>
    <qti-choice-interaction response-identifier="RESPONSE" shuffle="true" max-choices="1">
      <qti-simple-choice identifier="A">treatise</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="B">monograph</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="C">manifesto</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="D">essay</qti-simple-choice>
    </qti-choice-interaction>
      </qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>

    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-A" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! The card teaches that a treatise is &apos;long, formal&apos; and &apos;systematic.&apos; Eight wandering, joke-filled pages that chase memories are personal and loose — charming, but the opposite of a formal, systematic treatment.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-B" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! The card calls a monograph &apos;a scholarly study of one narrow topic, written by a specialist for specialists.&apos; An alumni magazine is a general audience, and reminiscence is not scholarship.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-C" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! A manifesto is a public declaration of aims and intentions, written to demand change. The coach demands nothing and declares no program — he is remembering, not campaigning.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-D" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Correct! An essay is a short prose piece that explores a subject from a personal angle, free to follow the writer&apos;s own turns of thought — which is exactly what these wandering, funny, memory-chasing pages are.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
  </qti-item-body>
  <qti-response-processing>
